course: dictionary
lesson: 7499
title: Postpone: moving things to later
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To postpone something means to move it to a later time instead of doing it now. «The match was postponed because of rain.» The match did not disappear. It was moved to a later day, so the players will still play it.
explain: Postpone is a verb: postpone, postpones, postponed, postponing. The words around it leave clues. «Postponed due to rain» tells you the reason, and «postpone until» tells you the new time.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In a formal notice, «The meeting has been postponed until further notice» means the meeting will happen later, but the new date is not yet known. If «moved to a later time» still makes sense in the sentence, you have it.
explain: In maths, a problem may say «the race was postponed by 3 days». Add the days to the old day to find the new one. If the race was on day 10, it is now on day 13.
fact: Postpone means to move an event to a later time instead of doing it now.
fact: Postponed does not mean cancelled: the event will still happen later.
fact: «Prepone» is Indian English and means move to an earlier time, the opposite of postpone.
fact: Useful phrases: «postpone until», «postponed due to rain», «postpone a decision».
fact: In a formal notice, «postponed until further notice» means the new date has not been decided yet.
exercise: «The match was postponed because of rain.» What does postponed mean here? | Won by the home team | Cancelled for ever | Played earlier, before the rain | *Moved to a later time
exercise: The race was postponed by 3 days. It was first planned for day 10. What day is it now? | Day 10 | Day 3 | *Day 13 | Day 7
exercise: Indian English speakers say "prepone". What does it mean? | Cancel the game for ever | Give a speech in a whisper | *Move to an earlier time, the opposite of postpone | Do what needs doing
test: The school trip was postponed due to illness. Will the trip still happen? | No, it is cancelled for ever | No, it was never planned | *Yes, at a later time | Yes, but it moves to an earlier time
test: Which phrase means to wait before you choose? | *postpone a decision | a servo | prepone a party | no cap
exam: «The meeting has been postponed until further notice.» What does this notice tell you? | The meeting is today | The meeting is cancelled for ever | The meeting has finished | *The meeting will happen later, on a date not yet decided
